# Code owners (A5-T10). Owner areas follow docs/architecture/00-overview.md §5.
#
# The LAST matching rule wins, so this file goes from broad to specific:
# repository-wide → agent areas → carve-outs inside them → contracts →
# security-critical paths (which must stay last).
#
# The repository belongs to a personal account, which has no teams, and GitHub
# silently ignores a rule whose owner does not resolve. So every rule names the
# account owner today; the comment on each line is the team it stands for.
# When the repository moves to an organization, replace @wouhliss with the team
# in the comment (e.g. @vgames/security).
#
# `cargo xtask codeowners check` (CI) fails if a tracked file has no owner or if
# a security-critical path resolves to a rule outside the security section.

# ---- repository-wide (orchestrator) ------------------------------------------
